From: Notebook OS <notebookos@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] ppd-cache: strip only TRAILING spaces from printer-make-and-model

_ppdCreateFromIPP2() sanitises printer-make-and-model before splitting it into
a make and a model. The comment says "Strip trailing whitespace", but the loop
that does it walks backwards over the whole string and has no exit condition,
so it replaces EVERY space with a NUL, not just the ones at the end:

    while (mptr > make)
    {
      mptr --;
      if (*mptr == ' ')
        *mptr = '\0';
    }

"Brother MFC-J1355DW" therefore becomes "Brother". The code immediately below
splits make and model on the first space, finds none left, and falls through to
its no-model-name case:

    else
      model = "Printer";

So every PPD generated from a printer's own IPP attributes — which is every
driverless queue, on any printer whose make and model contains a space, i.e.
all of them — comes out as:

    *Manufacturer: "Brother"
    *ModelName: "Printer"
    *NickName: "Printer - IPP Everywhere"

Stop at the first non-space, which is what "strip trailing whitespace" means
and what the surrounding code expects.

Signed-off-by: Notebook OS <notebookos@localhost>
---
 cups/ppd-cache.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/cups/ppd-cache.c b/cups/ppd-cache.c
--- a/cups/ppd-cache.c
+++ b/cups/ppd-cache.c
@@ -3293,6 +3293,8 @@
       mptr --;
       if (*mptr == ' ')
 	*mptr = '\0';
+      else
+        break;
     }
 
     if (!make[0])
